{
  "title": "AI cache stores unparseable responses forever",
  "description": "The AI client caches the raw provider response before the \
caller parses it (ramekin-core/src/ai/client.rs). When the provider returns a \
truncated or malformed response (e.g. gemini-2.5-flash occasionally stops \
after a few tokens: content '{\"normalized_title\": \"' with \
completion_tokens: 6), the garbage is cached permanently and every subsequent \
pipeline run fails that enrichment with 'AI call failed: Failed to parse \
response' without ever retrying the API. A scan on 2026-06-11 found ~30 such \
entries in normalize_title and generate_description, causing the persistent \
'Failed at save_recipe' tail in pipeline runs (these show up as enrichment \
failures counted against completed URLs in data/extraction-report.md).\n\
\n\
Suggested fix: validate that the response parses as the expected JSON shape \
before writing it to the cache (or let callers report parse failure so the \
client can evict the entry). A transient provider flake should be retried on \
the next run, not pinned forever.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pipeline",
    "ai",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-06-11T17:46:01-07:00",
